Diagnosis:
The issue is described in the bug report as an IllegalArgumentException when reading a CPIO archive generated by Redline RPM. The cause is that the Redline RPM creates CPIO archives where the trailer entry has a non-zero file mode, which violates an assumption in the reader.

From the test snippet, the failure occurs during iteration over entries in CpioArchiveInputStream.getNextEntry(), which calls getNextCPIOEntry(). Examining getNextCPIOEntry(), entries are read and returned until the trailer entry is reached, at which point getNextCPIOEntry() returns null.

In the method readNewEntry(boolean hasCrc), which reads one CPIO entry, the mode is read from the archive. If the mode is non-zero, it is set to the entry. Then, the entry name is read. If the mode is zero and the entry is not the trailer, an IOException is thrown stating mode zero is only allowed in the trailer.

However, the Redline RPM archive breaks this assumption by having a trailer entry with a non-zero mode. The current code does not handle this case properly and throws an IllegalArgumentException or IOException.

Thus, the root cause is that the code expects the trailer entry's mode to be zero, but Redline RPM generates archives where the trailer has non-zero mode, leading to an exception.

The relevant lines in readNewEntry reflect this:
```
330 :         long mode = readAsciiLong(8, 16);
331 :         if (mode != 0){
332 :             ret.setMode(mode);
333 :         }
...
347 :         if (mode == 0 && !name.equals(CPIO_TRAILER)){
348 :             throw new IOException("Mode 0 only allowed in the trailer. Found entry name: "+name);
349 :         }
```

The buggy assumption is here: only trailer entries are allowed to have mode zero, but Redline RPM violates this by setting non-zero mode on trailer entry.

The fix would involve relaxing this check to allow non-zero modes on trailer entry or properly handling this special case to not throw an exception.

No other recent bug reports are directly relevant to this CPIO trailer mode assumption.

Summary: The failure is due to an exception thrown when reading a CPIO entry whose name is the trailer name but has non-zero mode. The code assumes trailer mode is zero; this assumption is violated by Redline RPM archives. The exception occurs in the readNewEntry method validating this condition.

The patch referenced in the bug report likely relaxes or modifies this check.

